       "en": "To ask for directions, start with **“Excuse me”** and use **“How do I get to…?”**: **“Excuse me, how do I get to the post office?”**. Americans almost never say “Where is the way to…”. You can also ask **“Is there a pharmacy around here?”** or **“Is it far from here?”**. A very useful phrase is **“within walking distance”**: close enough to walk.",
